WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.310
Every contract ends.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.310
The only question is...

3
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.590
HOW?

4
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.660
Most end well.

5
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.940
Both sides do their part.

6
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:10.520
That's performance.

7
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.910
Or... one side lets the other

8
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.710
off. Someone new takes over.

9
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.890
A new deal replaces the old

10
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.230
one. Or two debts simply cancel

11
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:25.930
out.

12
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.480
If you end up owing YOURSELF

13
00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:30.440
— the debt is gone.

14
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.920
And after five years with no

15
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.900
claim? It's gone too.

16
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.450
Sometimes, no one is to blame.

17
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.170
The hall burns down before the

18
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.250
concert. That's frustration.

19
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.690
But — harder,

20
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.410
or dearer? That's NOT enough.

21
00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.280
And sometimes... someone breaks it.

22
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:57.240
Late. Badly. Or not at all.

23
00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.440
That's BREACH.

24
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.550
So what can you do?

25
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.150
Claim damages. Ask the court to

26
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.010
make them do it — or

27
00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.870
make them stop.

28
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.730
Cancel the deal.

29
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.350
Or hold back payment.

30
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.540
Born. Tested. Ended.

31
00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.380
That's... the Contract Line.
